title: "The Binding Test: Construction Audit, Synthetic Planning, and an Exploratory Feasibility Case Study of Causal Choice-Control Evaluation for AI Systems"
type: article
version: v1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-19
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22020047
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22020047"
authors:
  - family-names: Ryan
    given-names: Thomas
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, San Francisco, CA"
abstract: >-
  A methods and feasibility preprint introducing a block-yoked randomized
  design for testing whether later AI choice outputs depend on whether an
  earlier choice controlled the assigned history. The release separates a
  zero-call construction audit, conditional synthetic planning, and one
  nonconfirmatory provider feasibility trajectory.
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - AI evaluation
  - causal measurement
  - yoked control
  - choice contingency
  - large language models
  - construct validity
  - randomized evaluation
